# W24: "Load" on a GIF in the middle of a scrolled-back list, against the showcase scenario, as
# alexk in Couch Co-op's #general. The owner saw the whole message list go blank after that press on
# a real desktop; this keeps the list drawn through it, with real animated GIFs (the fake server's
# `/__fixtures/*.gif` is a four-frame GIF, so the app decodes, budgets and animates it).
# - Two GIF messages from priya and five text messages after them, then scrolled back so the first
#   GIF's Load card is mid-screen. Third-party pictures are off: both are Load cards.
# - Load: the setting goes on, the list keeps its place and the GIF draws in it (a blank list
#   draws no element), then animates. Shots are taken on the rig's clock, so each run's frame is
#   the same; the shots show the rows around it.
# The ids name the rows' seqs, which a fresh showcase server gives the same every run: the two
# GIFs posted here are 15728640 and 16777216 (the scenario's own GIF, from a host that never
# resolves, is 14680064 and shows its URL).

app 1280 800
window activate
wait idle
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username" within 5
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core connection connected
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core rows >= 14
wait idle

# 1. Two GIFs and five messages after them; scrolled back to the first GIF's Load card.
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"http://127.0.0.1:3999/__fixtures/first.gif\"}"
wait core w7 gif blocked within 10
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"http://127.0.0.1:3999/__fixtures/second.gif\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"after one\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"after two\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"after three\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"after four\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"after five\"}"
wait core text "after five"
wait idle
scroll message-gif-blocked-16777216 0 250
wait idle
wait core element message-gif-load-15728640
shot 01-scrolled-blocked

# 2. Load on the first GIF: on for everything, and the GIF drawn in place.
w7 mark
click message-gif-load-15728640
wait core w7 third-party on
expect settings /third_party_media true
wait core element message-gif-15728640 within 10
wait idle
expect core w7 new-requests Fixture_image >= 1
shot 02-loaded

# 3. Later on the rig's clock: the GIF has moved on a frame and the list is still drawn.
tick 250
wait idle
wait core element message-gif-15728640
shot 03-animated
